# will_search_pursuit — a visit walked for a will's search wants the searched target first
#
# Woodcraft wants four things; in the forest a search for its third ("buy seasoned wood") proposes,
# the nearest is its first — a branch to gather, one step from the entry. On the visit the search's
# trip ends in (Scene.WillPursuit), the will steers by the searched target alone: its plan is the
# five-step way to the charcoal burner, not the branch underfoot (`aim=3/4`, `pursuit=yes`). Its other
# targets stay within reach only by the three-step rule, when an object offers no way to the main one
# (WillPriority.WaysOn). The pursuit is the visit's: walking out and entering the same place again is
# an ordinary visit, and the will goes back to the nearest of its wants.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --grant-mm woodcraft

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60

click will-button
click will woodcraft
click want 2
wait 120
expect-state will-search "will-search state=proposed"
expect "Woodcraft: buy seasoned wood"
travel-go
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
expect-state will "aim=3/4"
expect-state will "pursuit=yes"

# Out, and in again: an ordinary visit, which wants the nearest.
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
expect-state will "aim=1/4"
expect-no-state will "pursuit=yes"
quit
